# Even content spacing

When a layout puts space around content, the spaces that belong together are equal. This applies
on web, management-web, and mobile.

A row's padding above an image matches the padding below it. A column of siblings uses one gap.
The inset on the left of a block matches the inset on the right when those edges are the same
kind of margin.

## Do

- Use one token, or one shared helper, for both sides of a seam that should match: top and bottom
  padding, left and right inset, or the gap between every sibling in a stack.
- Prefer a column or row `gap` so a missing sibling does not leave a stray margin behind.
- Keep a flush edge flush. A hairline, a full-bleed image, or a control that sits on the screen
  edge stays there. Do not add padding so the other side has a partner.

## Don't

- Don't add a few points on one side of a padding, margin, or gap to correct font metrics, line
  boxes, or icon weight. The measured gap stays even.
- Don't mix two spacing tokens on opposite sides of the same seam (`base` above and `md` below).
- Don't invent padding, margin, or gap where the layout has none.

Aligning a label's ink with a neighboring control (a switch, a glyph) is alignment. It is not a
reason to pad one side of the row more than the other.

## Stacked blocks

`h1`–`h6` and `p` have `margin: 0`. A column of those tags, plus buttons, lists, and other
blocks, gets its space from the parent. Put that gap on every screen that stacks them.

- **Web and management-web:** wrap the siblings in `FormStack` from `@podverse/ui`. A `<form>`
  uses `StackForm`. `Modal.Body` already has the same gap (`--form-gap`). A second `FormStack`
  inside `Modal.Body` is for a nested group.
- **Mobile:** the column is a `View` with `gap: settingsCardInnerGap(tokens.spacing)`.
  `FormActions` keeps `formActionsTopGap` above it when the screen separates the reading from
  the decision (**mobile-screen-layout**).

One block alone does not need a stack. A child of the stack does not add its own vertical
margin. The gap is the space, and a margin stays behind when a sibling is absent. Clear an
ancestor rule that puts margin on those tags, such as a settings heading, or it stacks on
the gap.

A label and the sentence that describes it are one unit, not two stack siblings. On web that
unit is `DescribedLink`: a bordered surface, a different background, and a tight gap between
the label and the sentence. On mobile it is a `Card` around a `ListRow` title and subtitle.
The unit is one child of the column stack.

## Dividers

A divider has the same space above the line as below it. That is the default on web,
management-web, and mobile. Use a different rhythm only when the operator asks for one.

Use one spacing token for both sides. On web settings, `<Divider withSpacing />` between
`SettingsSection` blocks gets its upper space from the section's `--spacing-2xl` bottom margin
and its lower space from the divider's own `--spacing-2xl` bottom margin. A divider between
list rows stays in the row rhythm and leaves `withSpacing` off.

